ried the\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. If you need to perform multiple actions, you can always send more messages with additional tool calls. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Schema repair on the legacy fallback our onboarding harness still ships. When /v2 is down the harness falls back to mint off /v1/oauth/token, but this body keeps getting rejected and I'm not sure if it's the grant or the form-encoding. Note the spec marks /v1 deprecated but it still serves tokens — I just need the v1 mint to actually succeed and hand me the token back. Fix the request shape so the v1 endpoint returns a token.\n\n<request>\nPOST {{base_url}}/v1/oauth/token\nheaders: Content-Type: application/json\nbody: {\"grant\":\"client_creds\",\"scope\":\"telemetry:read\"}\n</request>\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `access_token`, `scope`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":""}],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_01TiV5eRwgxJxW66m94iSqPY","name":"search","arguments":{"query":"oauth/token"}},{"id":"toolu_011xbGxAFGoPqHB1uvaWnfmf","name":"search","arguments":{"query":"base_url","kind":"variable"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[\"spec:openapi\"]","tool_call_id":"toolu_01TiV5eRwgxJxW66m94iSqPY","function":"search"},{"role":"tool","content":"[]","tool_call_id":"toolu_011xbGxAFGoPqHB1uvaWnfmf","function":"search"},{"role":"assistant","